.TH VORTAX 1 "2026" "vortax" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vortax \- run and manage QEMU virtual machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vortax
.I command
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads a system from a built-in catalog (or uses your own ISO, disk image or archive),
prepares its disk, starts it under QEMU and gives you VNC access, optionally through a tunnel.
KVM is used when available, software emulation (TCG) otherwise.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list, profiles
Show the system catalog and the hardware presets.
.TP
.B plan
Show what a run would do and the exact QEMU command. Changes nothing.
.TP
.B prepare, start, run
Download and set up a disk; start the VM in the background; or start it and stay in the foreground.
.TP
.B stop, kill, reboot, status, info
Control and inspect VMs.
.TP
.B password, snapshot, export, tunnel, edit, driver-iso, rm
Change the VNC password, manage qcow2 snapshots, export a disk (optionally with rclone), manage tunnels, change an existing VM's saved settings (RAM, CPUs, sound card) without touching its disk, build an ISO of drivers from a folder (and attach it), delete a VM.
.TP
.B wizard, preset
Interactive setup; save, list, show and remove named run presets. A preset name, catalog id or local file can be
given as the positional target of plan, prepare, start and run.
.TP
.B logs, screenshot, disk
Show or follow the QEMU log; save the guest display as a PNG; show, resize or compact a VM disk.
.TP
.B ssh, cp
For VMs started with --ssh: open a shell, or copy files with vm:PATH.
.TP
.B access
Install optional host remote-access programs (rdp, nomachine, rustdesk, anydesk).
.TP
.B dashboard
Serve the web dashboard (127.0.0.1:8765 by default, token protected).
.TP
.B doctor, selftest, check-links
Check the installation; boot a tiny test guest; check catalog URLs.
.SH OPTIONS WORTH KNOWING
.TP
.B --share PATH[:TAG]
Share a host folder over 9p. Repeatable.
.TP
.B --usb VID:PID
Pass a host USB device through. Repeatable.
.TP
.B --audio none|hda|ac97|sb16
Emulated sound card.
.TP
.B --ssh
Forward a free local port to the guest's port 22.
.TP
.B --snapshot-on-stop
Save the live state on stop and resume it on the next start (qcow2 disks).
.TP
.B --notify
Send a notification when the VM starts or stops.
.TP
.B --license
Print the license (GNU AGPL v3) and where the source is.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every run setting can be given as VORTAX_<NAME> (VORTAX_SYSTEM, VORTAX_TUNNEL, VORTAX_PASSWORD, ...).
Command line options override the environment, which overrides config.json.
.TP
.B VORTAX_HOME
Data directory (default ~/.local/share/vortax).
.TP
.B VORTAX_CONFIG
Config directory (default ~/.config/vortax).
.TP
.B TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY, NGROK_AUTHTOKEN
Tunnel credentials. They are never placed on a command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vortax/systems.json, profiles.json
Your own catalog entries; same schema as the built-in data, matched by id.
.SH SEE ALSO
qemu-system-x86_64(1), qemu-img(1)
